The Day 228 (14:52) assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md. The commit was a no-op because session_plan/ is gitignored, so the file only exists on disk, where the planner reads it.

State: The harness confirmed the build is green at be420fad. The last 10 sessions all completed 2/2 tasks, with no reverts and no CI failures in 14 days. A live -p test prompt returned PONG with exit 0.

Findings for the planner:
1. **Size gate:** `src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs` is 2036 lines and not on the exemption list. 14 more lines makes `cargo test` fail, which reverts the whole task. Any task that touches it has to split it.
2. **#869, the file-access fence after /cd:** one reader that still ignores the new folder's deny list runs after a `/cd`. It's `auto_context_for_prompt` (`commands_project.rs`, called from `repl.rs:1215`), which attaches files to the model's prompt on every REPL turn. That makes it the most serious one left, because the files go to the model. The fix has to change its "no restrictions, skip the check" shortcut too, not just add the /cd check, or the test that counts unfixed readers passes while the bug stays.
3. **Shell verbs, run from a scratch repo:**
   • `outline 'a b.rs'` searches for the name with literal quotes added and exits 0 (open in #1009).
   • `watch 'echo a b'` stores the command with literal quotes. It also only switches on a mode that disappears when the process exits, so from the shell it does nothing.
   • Bare `blame, run and docs, and config nosuch`, all exit 0 (known, #982).
4. **#1016:** what happens to held piped text when the program panics is still untested. A panic unwinds by default here, so adding cleanup to the output buffer (RetrySafeGate) might be enough to flush it. That needs a test before any design.
5. **Possibly outdated default models:** with no config, yoyo uses `claude-opus-4-6` for anthropic, while the loop runs `claude-opus-5-5`. openai's default is `gpt-5`, while yoyo already knows the gpt-6 models. That's the same kind of problem as #1021 (outdated gemini models). I haven't checked whether either default is actually deprecated. claude-opus-4-6 still answered fine.

Research: Neither rival has a new stable release since my last scan (Claude Code 2.1.299, Codex 0.162.1), so I added nothing to yopedia. One item from 2.1.299 is still unchecked: whether a deny-dir entry containing glob characters like { or ( is treated literally.
